WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.860
A car pulls away from a standing start.

2
00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:06.880
After t seconds it has
gone two t squared metres,

3
00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.110
and its graph curves upwards.

4
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.280
Its speedometer is covered.

5
00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:14.690
And a curve has no single rise over run.

6
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:18.730
So how fast is the car going
at exactly three seconds?

7
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.450
Is it the average over
the first three seconds?

8
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.270
Or is it simply how high the graph is?

9
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.600
In this mission, you'll draw a chord
from that point to a nearby one,

10
00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.340
then shrink the gap.

11
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.840
The chord gradients approach a limit.

12
00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:37.750
That limit is the derivative: the
curve's own gradient at one point.

13
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.610
Your mission: find how fast the car
is going at exactly three seconds.
